{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Parent\n\nEpic `77e3-28e2-31ec-47ec`, authorized at full scope by the operator on 2026-11-02.\nThis is deliverable 1 and the enabling dependency for the rest.\n\n## The gap, measured\n\nrebar's mechanism ratchet (`scripts/_mechanism_delta/`) asks \"is this mechanism\njustified?\", never \"is the system net-simpler afterward?\". Measured at `origin/main`\n`4cf1ae42946`:\n\n- `scripts/_mechanism_delta/compare.py:89-92` admits a `new` key on nothing more than a\n  nonblank in-tree marker.\n- `scripts/_mechanism_delta/markers.py:37-44` (`parse_marker`) yields exactly kind, name\n  and reason. Nothing parses a retirement.\n- `compare.py:99` never consults `counters.stale`, so removal is unconditionally allowed —\n  the shrink-only asymmetry.\n\nPlan review does not close the gap either. `A1` is the only complexity criterion and it is\nadvisory at `block_threshold` 0.95.\n\nSo a plan that adds a mechanism and retires nothing passes both gates.\n\n## The change\n\nAdd `project.net-mechanism`, a BLOCKING plan-review criterion in the `.rebar/` overlay. A\nplan adding an element of a counted kind must either name the mechanism it retires or\nstate why no retirement is possible. It reasons about the PLAN at claim time, before any\ncode exists — complementary to the ratchet, which reasons about the TREE at lint time.\n\nThe seven counted kinds are `lock`, `env_var`, `config_key`, `feature_flag`, `ci_gate`,\n`autouse_fixture`, `test_helper`, matching `scripts/_mechanism_delta`'s census exactly so\nthe criterion and the ratchet cannot drift apart on what counts.\n\n## Why a criterion rather than extending the ratchet\n\nThe ratchet runs on the tree, after the code is written. By then the mechanism exists and\nthe cost of removing it has been paid. The criterion runs at claim time against the plan,\nwhen the cheapest possible correction is available: rewrite a paragraph.\n\nThis is a `.rebar/` OVERLAY criterion, not a core one. It encodes this project's judgement\nabout its own mechanism growth and ships as project configuration, so another project\nadopting rebar does not inherit it.\n\n## Net-mechanism accounting for this change itself\n\nThis change adds ONE criterion to the overlay. It adds no lock, env var, config key,\nfeature flag, CI gate, autouse fixture or test helper — nothing in the counted set. It is\ntherefore net-zero against its own criterion, which is the honest answer rather than a\nclaimed retirement.\n\n## Portability\n\nPer the blocking `project.portability` criterion: this criterion runs inside plan review,\nwhich runs in-process wherever `rebar review-plan` runs. Its trigger is the gate, not a CI\nprovider, so it fires with no CI present. The rubric names no CI vendor, and an acceptance\ncriterion below asserts that absence by test.\n\n## Provider neutrality\n\nThe criterion is prompt-and-rubric only. It names no provider, no model and no\nprovider-specific capability, so it runs under whatever provider the project configures.\nrebar must support a wide variety of providers and models, and a criterion that assumed\none would violate that. Verified by the frontmatter and rubric tests below, which assert\non structure rather than on any provider's behaviour.\n\n## Where it goes\n\n- The criterion id and its routing live in the `.rebar/` overlay, read through\n  `registry.effective_criteria` and `effective_routing`.\n- The rubric body is a prompt resolved by `prompts.get_prompt` under\n  `criterion_prompt_id(\"project.net-mechanism\")`.\n- Routing is exercised through `route_criteria`, the same entry point production uses.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] `registry.effective_criteria(REPO_ROOT)` contains `project.net-mechanism`.\n- [x] `effective_routing(REPO_ROOT)[\"project.net-mechanism\"][\"default_posture\"]` is\n      `\"blocking\"`.\n- [x] `prompts.get_prompt(criterion_prompt_id(\"project.net-mechanism\"), repo_root=REPO_ROOT)`\n      resolves to a non-empty body.\n- [x] `parse_front_matter` on that body yields all six keys.\n- [x] `route_criteria` returns `project.net-mechanism` for a plan in its declared scope.\n- [x] The rubric body contains a `## Finding threshold` heading.\n- [x] The rubric body contains a `## Required finding fields` heading.\n- [x] The rubric body contains a `## Non-findings` heading.\n- [x] The rubric body names all seven kinds as literal strings.\n- [x] The rubric body contains none of `GitHub Actions`, `GitLab`, `Jenkins`, `CircleCI`,\n      `Travis`.\n- [x] `make verify` exits 0.\n\n## Measurement base\n\nEvery citation and count above was read from `origin/main` at `4cf1ae42946`."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793684322562656389,"uuid":"7d773a27-2b9e-4577-b1d0-466fc27f2f54"}